# Everything the diagram interchange owes a shape or an edge. One row per drawn element.
#
# Every drawn element is here
#   Including the three that are worked out. A `group`, an `association` and a `textAnnotation` are
#   each computed from the primitives' boxes, and they are here all the same, because this relation
#   carries no `x` and no `y` for anything. It says which elements owe a shape, never where the
#   shape is, so a row here files no coordinate, and working the coordinates out stays in
#   `examples/diagramming`, which computes the primitives' geometry anyway.
#
# No row, no diagram interchange
#   An element with no row here gets no diagram interchange, so `examples/rendering` must work out
#   its geometry a second time from the artifact it just read, and any other reader loses it
#   quietly: missing DI is not an error, it is nothing drawn.
#
# The same test `eliminations/derived.sqlc` passes
#   And the test still bites. A figure that can be worked out must not be filed; a coordinate that
#   can be worked out must not be filed either. Neither is filed here. Working one out into an
#   artifact is what both stages do, and the test was never about that.
#
# `di` is declared
#   BPMN has two carriers, and they are not interchangeable. A box is a `bpmndi:BPMNShape` with
#   `dc:Bounds`; a route is a `bpmndi:BPMNEdge` with `di:waypoint`s, in a third namespace. An
#   association is the only thing here that is a route, and counting it with the boxes would make
#   the count of shapes a number that matches nothing in the document.
-- BPMN 2.0 DI: a bpmndi:BPMNShape per box and a bpmndi:BPMNEdge per route.
SELECT p.filing AS document, 'pool' AS shape_of, p.filing AS subject, 'shape' AS di
FROM ( :compose(diagrams/pools.sqlc) ) p
UNION ALL
SELECT l.filing, 'lane', l.layer, 'shape'
FROM ( :compose(layers/every_layer.sqlc) ) l
UNION ALL
SELECT o.filing, 'task', o.label, 'shape'
FROM ( :compose(entries/operations.sqlc) ) o
UNION ALL
SELECT c.composition, 'callActivity', c.composed_layer || '<-' || c.part_filing || '/' || c.part_layer, 'shape'
FROM ( :compose(diagrams/foreign_calls.sqlc) ) c
UNION ALL
SELECT k.filing, 'group', k.layer, 'shape'
FROM ( :compose(diagrams/categories.sqlc) ) k
UNION ALL
SELECT g.filing, 'textAnnotation', g.note, 'shape'
FROM ( :compose(diagrams/legends.sqlc) ) g
UNION ALL
SELECT d.filing, 'association', d.from_layer || '->' || d.to_layer, 'edge'
FROM ( :compose(diagrams/dependences.sqlc) ) d
